"Nadia's family arrived in Sydney with three suitcases and no friends. On their first evening, as they sat on the floor of an empty flat, there was a knock at the door. It was the old neighbour from downstairs, holding a pot of hot rice and dal. She did not ask where they were from, what they believed, or whether they would ever pay her back. She simply said, “You must be tired,” and left the pot on the doorstep.",
