"For his birthday, Bilal was given a whole shelf in the living room: “This is your shelf,” his parents said. He arranged his books, his cricket ball and a small model plane. For a week he felt like the owner of the world.",
"Then the family moved house. The landlord sold the flat, the shelf went into a skip, and Bilal realised that even his parents had only been renting. The landlord, in turn, had a mortgage to the bank. And the bank answered to the government. Everyone who seemed to own something was holding it only for a while.",
