"On the bus home, their teacher, Ms Rahman, talked about Al-Quddus, the Most Holy. “The snow was beautiful,” she said, “but it was clean only until someone touched it, and it melted by evening. Everything we call pure in this world is pure for a while, or pure compared with something dirtier. Al-Quddus is far above every fault and every shortcoming — not 'clean for now', not 'better than most', but free of any imperfection at all.”",
